; JSONC's transducer part: the document's JSON events from the jsonc
; grammar's rule passes (ParserEvents/1), streamed as the parser makes
; them, so that a host that reads parser events (alchemy-cli's translate
; and run --grammar, aless) reads a JSONC document through this file rather
; than through transduce's inference over the grammar's rule events.
;
; The grammar is json's with comments, and trailing commas where the
; grammar allows them, taken by the lexer and the rules before any pass
; reaches the part, so the rules that remain map onto a tree as json's
; do, and the part is the library's declarative transducer, transduce-tree,
; with json's spec keyed by rule name: a map rule's open pass begins an
; object and its close pass ends it, a list rule's an array; a pair rule's
; open pass announces the member's name, its first token's value; and a
; val rule's open pass yields the scalar its first token carries, with the
; lexeme a number token keeps (2.50 is written 2.50). A document holding
; no value, comments alone, is one null, as the grammar reads it. Every
; event is the one the walk of the grammar's value gives, a number's
; lexeme aside, which alchemy-cli's transduce.tsv runner holds it to; a
; repeated member is streamed twice, as the document spells it, for a
; tree-contract or a capture's policy to judge.
def jsonc-transduce [input]
  transduce-tree
    record
      entry :map (record (entry :container :object))
      entry :list (record (entry :container :array))
      entry :pair (record (entry :key 0))
      entry :val (record (entry :scalar 0))
    input
